<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia's November palm oil exports 700,566t - SGS.</title>
<headline>Malaysia's November palm oil exports 700,566t - SGS.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargo surveyor Societe Generale de Surveillance (SGS) Malaysia Sdn Bhd said it estimated Malaysia's palm oil exports for November at 700,566 tonnes against 736,374 tonnes in October.</p>
<p>It said the exports comprised 200,040 tonnes of RBD palm oil, 264,682 tonnes of RBD palm olein and 78,363 tonnes of RBD palm stearin. The other products accounted for 157,481 tonnes.  </p>
<p>China, which was the main buyer during the period, took 105,600 tonnes, India at 79,943 tonnes, Pakistan at 70,088 and Egypt at 46,440 tonnes.</p>
<p>Countries in the European Union bought 86,689 tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-230-8911)</p>
